Found under k291 (2026-10-31). Since k291, `OCP::Cmd::Apply::CR::ensure_crds` leaves a cluster CRD that declares fields this ocp does not know (newer than this ocp) as it is, so the API server does not drop those fields from every OCPNode. `OCP::Cmd::DeployRobocop::_apply_manifests` (ocp deploy-robocop) still writes the OCPNode/OCPNodeProvider CRDs via `ensure()` with no such check, so an older ocp running deploy-robocop overwrites a newer CRD.

Done = deploy-robocop judges each CRD by `OCP::Drift->crd_schema_diff` like ensure_crds (one shared helper, not a copy), prints the same `[skip] … newer than this ocp` line, and a test shows a newer CRD is left alone and an older one is updated.

